  "description": {
   "value": "<p><strong>Cost:</strong> 750eb (Expensive)</p>\n<p><em>The popular, mass-market Sandevistan OS from Zetatech. It's widely praised by users for its minimalism and ease-of-use.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Sandevistan Operating System.</strong> The Sandevistan can now be activated as half of a ROF 2 Action, but its duration is reduced to 15 seconds (5 Rounds). While active, in addition to Sandevistan’s usual +3 bonus to Initiative, the user gains a +1 bonus to REF, which can increase REF above 8 and does not stack with Synthcoke. After the Sandevistan’s duration ends, it cannot be activated again for an hour unless the user voluntarily suffers 2 Humanity Loss per consecutive activation before an hour passes (e.g., 2 -&gt; 4 -&gt; 6, etc).</p>\n<p><em>NOTE: Credit to Infernox for the basis and concept of this OS.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Enhances:</strong> Sandevistan<br>\n<strong>Option Slots:</strong> 0 (Cyberware Enhancement)</p>\n<p><strong>Foundry notes:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Every Operating System is incompatible with every other Operating System and with the base cyberware it is for: none of them can be installed while another OS, or that OS's own base cyberware, is anywhere in the user's body or in a worn apparatus they're connected to. The sheet doesn't enforce that.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>From <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13EnSAoiLDsC7zmL-Jr1RqIh_EnuVuFnExqiipDVquMk/edit\">Corgo's 77 Collection V3</a> by Corgopolis (Operating Systems &gt; Sandevistan Operating Systems).</em></p>"
  },
